-- title:
--   Away-unit groups are monotone in the lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rational numbers, so that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is the associated quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $R$ and $R'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $R' \le R$, and let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is the inclusion of subgroups $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R'\,v \le \mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v$ inside $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])^{\times}$. Here, for a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$, the subgroup $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,\Lambda\,v$ is by definition the infimum, over all height-one primes $w \neq v$, of the preimage under `CosetGraph.toLoc w` of the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) $\Lambda\,w$; the map `CosetGraph.toLoc w` is the homomorphism of unit groups induced by the inclusion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ into the local algebra at $w$, and [`Submodule.localBoxUnits`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) $\Lambda\,w$ is the set of units $u$ of that local algebra with both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ lying in the additive subgroup [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\,w$, the local completion of $\Lambda$ at $w$, which is generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$. Thus a unit of the quaternion algebra which is a local unit for $R'$ at every finite place other than $v$ is a local unit for $R$ at every such place.
--
--   This is the elementary monotonicity property of the groups of $v$-away local units of a lattice in a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, used to transport units of a suborder into the away-unit group of a larger order. It is invoked in the construction of an element of prescribed reduced norm in the intersection of level subgroups attached to an Eichler order and the meet order used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
